claude-code-writer (builtin, external-cli:claude ✓): Description: Explicit file-writing Claude Code CLI mode; requires local authentication and trusted user settings/hooks; Tools: default/ambient; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- codex-exec (builtin, external-cli:codex ✓): Description: Read-only one-shot analysis through the installed Codex CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- codex-exec-writer (builtin, external-cli:codex ✓): Description: Explicit workspace-writing one-shot execution through the installed Codex CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- cursor-agent (builtin, external-cli:cursor-agent ✓): Description: Read-only one-shot analysis through the installed Cursor CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- cursor-agent-writer (builtin, external-cli:cursor-agent ✓): Description: Explicit workspace-writing one-shot execution through the installed Cursor CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- delegate (builtin): Description: Lightweight subagent that inherits the parent model with no default reads; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, edit, write, contact_supervisor; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- evidence-auditor (builtin): Description: Independent evidence reviewer for checking whether important research claims are supported by their sources; Tools: read, web_search, fetch_content, get_search_content, source_check; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- oracle (builtin, context: fork, aliases: advisor): Description: High-context decision-consistency oracle that protects inherited state and prevents drift; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- researcher (builtin): Description: Autonomous web researcher — searches, evaluates, and synthesizes a focused research brief; Tools: read, write, web_search, fetch_content, get_search_content, source_check; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: medium\n- reviewer (builtin): Description: Versatile review specialist for code diffs, plans, proposed solutions, codebase health, and PR/issue validation; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, contact_supervisor; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- scout (builtin): Description: Fast codebase recon that returns compressed context for handoff; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, write, contact_supervisor; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: low\n- worker (builtin, context: fork, aliases: developer, coder, implementer, develop): Description: Implementation agent for normal tasks and approved oracle handoffs; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, edit, write, contact_supervisor; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high","tool_call_id":"call_5c9ab2a8cf2bf9e082d9680b79015d20"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Scout agents are available. Launching 4 parallel scouts via one workflow to map the rebuild: (1) reference repo anatomy, (2) extracted 0.44.0 sources, (3) 0.18→0.44 delta, (4) native/renderer surface.","reasoning_content":"User wants subagent scouting. Plan: launch parallel scouts to survey:\n1. Reference repo structure (`refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main`) — how the reconstruction is organized, build toolchain, what `source/` contains, manifests, scripts.\n2. The 0.44.0 extracted app (`analysis/extracted` + sections) — diff surface vs 0.18, what's new/changed.\n3. Possibly native binaries + renderer.\n\nPer workflow guidance: one top-level subagent workflow call with async:true, children launch inside it. Use builtin `scout` agents. I should write a workflow script.\n\nLet me define 3-4 scouts:\n- scout-a: reference repo anatomy (dirs, build scripts, package.json, how sources map to app.asar, manifests/tests)\n- scout-b: 0.44.0 extracted sources inventory (dist structure, entry modules, size, what's new vs the RE-REPORT)\n- scout-c: reference → 0.44 delta mapping: which subsystems in reference need updating (compare 0.18 source/ modules against 0.44 sections)\n- scout-d: native/sidecar + renderer assets.\n\nOutputs written to files (scouts have write). Use runs.run with output paths maybe. Keep simple: each scout returns inline summary and writes a findings file under analysis/rebuild-scout/.\n\nActually scout agents have tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, write. Good.\n\nWorkflow script: launch 4 scouts in parallel via runs.all, await, then return summaries. Use async:true (default asyncByDefault true). Then when they complete, I get notified natively. Since I want results back in this turn, I can await runs.all in the script — but with async:true the workflow returns immediately and children run in background, then the parent session gets woken. Actually the script awaits runs.all inside... For async workflows, the script runs and awaits; results come back when complete. Let me just do the workflow with async:true and the script awaiting all runs. The workflow returns control immediately but the session is woken on completion? For async composites, parent gets results when done. Simplest: single workflow call, script does runs.all awaited, returns the summaries.\n\nLet me write it.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_355a3b1e051709bc0fb84f6281c60b02","type":"function","function":{"name":"subagent","arguments":"{\"async\":true,\"workflowScript\":\"const roots = {\\n  work: '/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot',\\n  ref: '/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main',\\n};\\n\\nconst outDir = roots.work + '/analysis/rebuild-scout';\\nawait runs.run('scout-ref-anatomy', {agent:'scout', task:`Survey the reference reconstruction repo at ${roots.ref}. This is a source-oriented reconstruction of Grok Bot 0.18.0. Map: (1) top-level layout and role of each dir (source/, src/, frontend/, manifests/, scripts/, tests/, patches/, docs/); (2) how source/ is organized per-process (electron-main, electron-preload, host, coordinator, local-exec-daemon, box-exec-daemon, node-agent-coordinator, packages, internal) — list key files and approx line counts per dir; (3) the build/packaging toolchain in scripts/ and package.json — how sources are compiled and assembled back into a .app (electron-builder? custom?), how the shipped renderer is pinned/transformed, and how chunk-hash verification works; (4) how PROVENANCE/manifests record upstream artifacts; (5) any version gates or 0.18-specific constants that a 0.44.0 rebuild must change. Write your findings to ${outDir}/scout-ref-anatomy.md and return a compact summary (<=30 lines) with the 5 most load-bearing facts for reusing this repo as the scaffold for a 0.44.0 rebuild.`});\\n\\nawait runs.run('scout-044-sources', {agent:'scout', task:`Survey the extracted 0.44.0 app sources at ${roots.work}/analysis/extracted and ${roots.work}/analysis/app.asar.unpacked (extracted from Grok_Bot_0.44.0.dmg). Map: (1) dist/ tree — entry modules (main.cjs, main-core.cjs, main-app.cjs, utilityProcess coordinator, local-exec-daemon), their sizes and minified/bundled state; (2) dist/native — each Mach-O .node/.helper binary, type, size; (3) package.json of the asar — deps, workspaces, version fields; (4) which sources look like plain readable JS vs bundled/minified; (5) any source maps (.map files). Do NOT deep-read minified code. Write findings to ${outDir}/scout-044-sources.md and return a compact summary (<=30 lines): what raw material exists for a rebuild and its biggest gaps (e.g., missing source maps, minified bundles).`});\\n\\nawait runs.run('scout-delta-018-044', {agent:'scout', task:`Delta-scout between the 0.18 reconstruction sources (${roots.ref}/source and ${roots.ref}/src) and the 0.44.0 analysis evidence (${roots.work}/analysis/RE-REPORT.md, ${roots.work}/analysis/sections/sec-*.md, ${roots.work}/analysis/extracted). For each major subsystem in the reference (electron-main, electron-preload, host, node-agent-coordinator, local-exec-daemon, box-exec-daemon, packages, frontend): state whether 0.44 evidence indicates it is unchanged, evolved, or new. Flag specifically: bundle id/track constants, update feed URLs, new 0.44 features (voice calls, webauthn signer, CUGrokBotService, cookie import, 1Password launcher, grokbot:// template deep links, anyrun protocol, GrokBotService vs SandBoxService) and which have no counterpart in the 0.18 source tree. Use grep on both trees; do not read whole files. Write findings to ${outDir}/scout-delta-018-044.md and return a compact summary (<=30 lines): the subsystem-by-subsystem verdict table plus the top 10 new-in-0.44 items needing fresh reconstruction.`});\\n\\nawait runs.run('scout-native-render', {agent:'scout', task:`Scout two surfaces of the 0.44.0 build at ${roots.work}/analysis. (A) Native/sidecar: list every binary under analysis/app.asar.unpacked/dist/native and analysis/extracted/dist/deps — for each, run file + lipo -info + (for Mach-O) strings | head -40 to identify language (Rust/Go/C), role, and whether the 0.18 reference (${roots.ref}) ships an equivalent under its source/ or scripts/; note the Rust webauthn signer and op-launcher in particular and whether the 0.18 tree has Rust sources. (B) Renderer: find the renderer bundles (index-*.js under analysis/extracted/dist), the i18n lingui catalog, and any source maps; compare against ${roots.ref}/frontend (what the 0.18 reconstruction kept as readable frontend) and ${roots.ref}/scripts renderer-pin/transform tooling. Write findings to ${outDir}/scout-native-render.md and return a compact summary (<=30 lines): per-binary verdict (reuse 0.18 source / re-derive / treat as opaque binary) and the renderer strategy options for 0.44.`});\\n\\nconst [refA, srcA, deltaA, natA] = await runs.all([\\n  {key:'scout-ref-anatomy'}, {key:'scout-044-sources'}, {key:'scout-delta-018-044'}, {key:'scout-native-render'},\\n]);\\nreturn { refAnatomy: refA, sources044: srcA, delta: deltaA, nativeRender: natA };\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"Run fan-out: 0/64 used, 64 remaining\nAsync workflow [83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c]\n\nThe async run is detached and running in the background.\nYou are in an interactive session. Return control to the user now; Pi will wake you through the native completion notification when this subagent completes or needs attention. Do not run sleep/polling loops to wait for this async subagent; it does not need a wait call.\nUse bg_wait only for provider, detached, or other background work that lacks a native completion notification.\nIf the current turn must receive results from work without a native notification before it ends, call blocking bg_wait(); ordinary async subagent runs do not need a wait call because their completion is delivered natively.\nOtherwise, continue any independent work or return control to the user. Use subagent({ action: \"status\", id: \"...\" }) for a one-shot status/result or to inspect a blocked/stale run, never as a wait loop.\nMission: ebad976b-271c-460a-a8d8-61b67776b4d3 (active)","tool_call_id":"call_355a3b1e051709bc0fb84f6281c60b02"},{"role":"assistant","content":"4 scouts dispatched in parallel (run `83b3ebe0`, mission active). They're writing findings to `analysis/rebuild-scout/*.md`:\n\n1. **scout-ref-anatomy** — 0.18 reference repo: layout, build toolchain, how sources reassemble into a .app\n2. **scout-044-sources** — extracted 0.44.0 asar/native inventory: what raw material exists\n3. **scout-delta-018-044** — subsystem-by-subsystem delta verdict + top new-in-0.44 items\n4. **scout-native-render** — per-binary reuse verdict (Rust signer, op-launcher) + renderer strategy\n\nI'll report back with a rebuild plan once they complete."},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow child completed: **scout-ref-anatomy**\nWorkflow run: 83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c\nChild run: 32ea0b37-53b3-4c92-bd8f-e9d72de464c5\nOutput: /Users/panda/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-panda-Projects-test-local-grok-bot--/subagent-artifacts/outputs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c/context.md\nStatus: workflow still running"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":"Scout 1/4 done (`scout-ref-anatomy`). Findings at `analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-ref-anatomy.md`. Still waiting on: 044-sources, delta-018-044, native-render — will consolidate the rebuild plan when all three land.","reasoning_content":"One of four scouts completed. Wait for the rest — return control? The wake is per-child. I should just acknowledge briefly and continue waiting; other children will wake me. Give a compact status."},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow child completed: **scout-044-sources**\nWorkflow run: 83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c\nChild run: bbe64187-187f-43a8-866e-6593b09f1b7d\nOutput: /Users/panda/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-panda-Projects-test-local-grok-bot--/subagent-artifacts/outputs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c/scout-044-sources.md\nStatus: workflow still running"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":"Scout 2/4 done (`scout-044-sources`). 2 remaining: delta-018-044, native-render."},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow child completed: **scout-delta-018-044**\nWorkflow run: 83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c\nChild run: 80df9860-691e-47df-97b5-68931c51a33d\nOutput: /Users/panda/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-panda-Projects-test-local-grok-bot--/subagent-artifacts/outputs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c/scout-delta-018-044.md\nStatus: workflow still running"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":"Scout 3/4 done (`scout-delta-018-044`). 1 remaining: native-render."},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow child completed: **scout-native-render**\nWorkflow run: 83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c\nChild run: 8ca859cb-25c9-430e-9185-09e3e57fff74\nOutput: /Users/panda/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-panda-Projects-test-local-grok-bot--/subagent-artifacts/outputs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c/scout-native-render.md\nStatus: workflow still running"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":"All 4 scouts done. Reading findings now.","reasoning_content":"All 4 children done; workflow may still be wrapping up. Let me read the 4 findings files and synthesize. The workflow status says \"still running\" — probably just finishing. I can read the files now.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_201d163a28993bf83f2636e89997bbfa","type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"cd \\\"/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/rebuild-scout\\\" && ls -la && wc -l *.md 2>/dev/null\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"total 56\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 5 panda  staff    160 Sep 14 15:01 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 9 panda  staff    288 Sep 14 14:51 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 panda  staff   6721 Sep 14 14:58 scout-delta-018-044.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 panda  staff   5638 Sep 14 15:01 scout-native-render.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 panda  staff  10231 Sep 14 14:52 scout-ref-anatomy.md\n      47 scout-delta-018-044.md\n      39 scout-native-render.md\n      73 scout-ref-anatomy.md\n     159 total\n","tool_call_id":"call_201d163a28993bf83f2636e89997bbfa"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background task failed: **workflow**\nWorkflow receipt: /var/folders/fs/brn3wr_x4ns2km1cq1ph9zb80000gn/T/pi-subagents-uid-501/async-subagent-runs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c/workflow-receipt.json\n\nError: Duplicate workflow key 'scout-ref-anatomy' used with incompatible launch params.\n    at validateRunCall ([worker eval]:637:65)\n    at launchRunsAll ([worker eval]:693:5)\n    at Object.all ([worker eval]:736:33)\n    at workflow-script.js:16:47\n    at async MessagePort.<anonymous> ([worker eval]:979:15)\n\nChild outputs:\n- key=scout-ref-anatomy run=32ea0b37-53b3-4c92-bd8f-e9d72de464c5 status=completed\n  Saved output: /Users/panda/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-panda-Projects-test-local-grok-bot--/subagent-artifacts/outputs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c/context.md\n  Preview:\n    | # Scout: grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed anatomy (scaffold candidate for 0.44.0 rebuild)\n    | \n    | Repo: `/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main`\n    | Node engines `>=26.5.0 <27`; Electron devDep 42.1.0 (dev only — the shipped 0.18 shell is reused at package time); esbuild 0.28.2 bundler; TypeScript 7.0.2; vite for the reconstructed frontend only. **No electron-builder** — packaging is a fully custom Node pipeline.\n    | \n    | ## 1. Top-level layout\n    | \n    | - `source/` — readable reconstructed TypeScript for all runtime processes (~80 KB LOC; see §2).\n    | - `src/app/` — the *staged upstream app payload*: `package.json` (name `sand`, version **0.18.0**, main `dist/electron-main/main.cjs`, `@anysphere/*` workspace deps) plus `dist/` hydrated from the checksum-pinned upstream `app.asar` by bootstrap (`scripts/lib/runtime.mjs:hydrateSourcePayloadFromAsar`). This is the asar staging root.\n    | - `frontend/` — partial evidence-backed reconstruction of the renderer (React/vite: `src/main.tsx`, `src/production/`, `src/recovered/`, `src/upstream.ts`, `manifests/renderer-*.json`). Used only for the \"clean-source\" renderer mode; NOT the shipped UI.\n    | - `manifests/reconstruction/` — `electron-main-production-bindings-manifest.json`, `renderer-closure.json`, `runner-parity-audit.json` (audit inputs, not build config).\n    | - `scripts/` — the entire build/package/verify toolchain (~7.4k LOC across 20 `.mjs` + `lib/`).\n    | - `tests/` — `node --test` suite (`node --test tests/*.test.mjs`): packaging, publication-bootstrap, updater-guard, router-settings, MCP/exec, inference-router tests.\n    | - `patches/` — one patchfile (`@connectrpc__connect@1.6.1.patch`) applied by `apply-third-party-patches.mjs` on postinstall.\n    | - `docs/` — `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PUBLISHING.md`, assets.\n    | - `research-archives/original/0.18.0/` — Git LFS preservation of the macOS arm64 DMG + Windows installer + `artifacts.json` + SHA256SUMS.\n    | - `PROVENANCE.md` (repo root) — upstream artifact identity & evidence-only rules.\n    | \n    | ## 2. source/ per-process organization (ts LOC)\n    | \n    | | dir | ~LOC | key files |\n    | |---|---|---|\n    | | `electron-main/` | 16.3k | `main.ts`, `main-edge.ts`, `main-production-services.ts`, `production-binding-providers.ts`, `production-ipc-contract.ts`, subdirs: account, auth, box, coordinator, mcp, secrets, update, vnc, window-*, startup, telemetry, generated |\n    | | `electron-preload/` | 1.6k | `preload.ts` + `runtime/{primary,dev-controls,webview,vnc}.ts` entrypoints |\n    | | `electron-dev-controls/` | 167 | `main.ts` |\n    | | `host/` | **64.8k** (largest hand-written) | `main.ts`, `host-gateway-api.ts`, `gateway-server.ts`, `host-runner-composition.ts`, `sand-host.ts`, `sand-multitask.ts`, agents/, runner/, box/, local-exec/, mcp-auth/, storage/, workflows/ |\n    | | `node-agent-coordinator/` | 3.4k | `main.ts` (composeCoordinator), `inference-router.ts`, `renderer-port-server.ts`, `client-side-tool-v2-relay.ts`, `control-port-client.ts`, oauth/, gateway/, telemetry/ |\n    | | `local-exec-daemon/` | 514 | `main.ts` (runLocalExecDaemonEntrypoint) |\n    | | `box-exec-daemon/` | 537 | `main.ts`, `cli.ts` |\n    | | `packages/` | 337k | 31 `@anysphere/*` workspace libs: agent, agent-core, agent-exec, chat-inference(+proto), context(+rpc), mcp-core, proto, redaction, shell-exec, prompt-jsx, metrics, hooks*, etc. (mostly generated/proto-heavy) |\n    | | `shared/` | 16k | cross-process contracts: `transcript.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `local-exec-*.ts`, `gateway-wire.ts`, `inference-router.ts`, `update.ts`, rpc/, observability/ |\n    | | `internal/` | 426 | small internals |\n    | \n    | ## 3. Build/packaging toolchain (custom, no electron-builder)\n    | \n    | Pipeline (`npm run package` = check → `scripts/package-macos.mjs`):\n    | \n    | 1. **bootstrap** (`scripts/bootstrap-runtime.mjs`) — downloads (or uses Git-LFS archive copy of) `Grok_Bot_0.18.0.dmg`, verifies SHA-256, mounts via hdiutil, caches `.cache/runtime/Grok Bot.app`, and extracts upstrea