ry | Type | Language | Role | 0.18 equivalent |\n    | |---|---|---|---|---|\n    | | `sand-op-launcher` | Mach-O universal (x86_64 + arm64), executable | Native (no Rust/Swift runtime strings found; small hardened launcher) | Hardened launcher/wrapper for 1Password CLI (`op`): codesign-verifies `com.1password.op` (team `2BUA8C4S2C`), sandbox_init profile restricting App Data access, env scrubbing (`OP_CACHE=false`, `OP_BIOMETRIC_UNLOCK_ENABLED=true`, `OP_LOAD_DESKTOP_APP_SETTINGS=false`), `account list --format=json`, service-account token creation. Strings: \"untrusted 1Password CLI\", \"1Password CLI changed before launch\" | **TS orchestration exists, launcher binary itself does not.** 0.18 has `source/electron-main/onepassword/onepassword-cli-runtime.ts` + `onepassword-cli-dev-controls.ts` which *expect* a launcher at `dist/native/` and codesign-verify it (constant `SAND_OP_LAUNCHER_IDENTIFIER_REQUIREMENT = 'identifier \"sand-op-launcher\"'`). No Rust/launcher source in the 0.18 tree (`find -name '*.rs'` = none) |\n    | | `sand-webauthn-signer` | Mach-O universal (x86_64 + arm64), executable | **Rust** (strings show `crates/sand-webauthn-signer/src/main.rs`, aes 0.8.4 / getrandom crates, `sand-release-cargo-home`, built on Anysphere Buildkite CI) | CTAP2/FIDO2 security-key signer: parse DER/CBOR (`IndefiniteLengthTagNumber`, `unexpected key`), operations makeCred/getAssertion, PIN/UV states (`PresenceRequired`, `force_pin_change`, `UserVerification`), emits signer-event lines | **TS side only.** 0.18 `source/node-agent-coordinator/webauthn/signer.ts` (line 47: `SIGNER_BINARY = ... \"sand-webauthn-signer\"`) spawns and parses this binary's event stream (presence-required / pin-not-set / pin-blocked / uv-* events match the Rust binary's strings exactly). No Rust sources (`crates/sand-webauthn-signer`) in the 0.18 tree — only the consumer. 0.18 `scripts/verify.mjs` line 58 merely requires the *built binary* to exist |\n    | \n    | **Verdict:** both native executables are **opaque binaries — treat as prebuilt, reuse from 0.44 build as-is** (they are self-contained, codesigned wrappers/signers). The *Node-side protocol* is fully recoverable from 0.18 TS sources (`signer.ts`, `onepassword-cli-runtime.ts`), so integration glue can be rebuilt; the Rust crates cannot (sources never published).\n    | \n    | ### `analysis/extracted/dist/deps/`\n    | \n    | | Entry | Contents | 0.18 equivalent |\n    | |---|---|---|\n    | | `cursor-proclist` | dir; `build/Release/cursor_proclist.node` — native Node addon (C/C++) | 0.18 has `scripts/build-tree-sitter-*.mjs` etc.; check `scripts/lib/*` + `patches/` — proclist addon is buildable via node-gyp if source in patches; else opaque |\n    | | `tree-sitter` | `build/Release/tree_sitter_runtime_binding.node` (node-gyp C addon) | 0.18 `scripts/build-tree-sitter-electron.mjs` + `build-tree-sitter-node.mjs` — **rebuildable from source** |\n    | | `tree-sitter-bash` | `prebuilds/darwin-arm64/tree-sitter-bash.node` | Same tree-sitter tooling; prebuild = stock npm package artifact |\n    | | `web-tree-sitter` | JS + `tree-sitter.wasm` | Stock npm package — reuse |\n    | | `node-addon-api`, `node-gyp-build` | Pure-JS npm helpers | Stock — reuse |\n    | | `runtime-deps-manifest.json` | Records required/copied/nodeFiles lists (see above) | Matches 0.18 packaging flow |\n    | \n    | ## B. Renderer\n    | \n    | - **Bundle:** `analysis/extracted/dist/renderer/assets/index-C6zjACOA.js` (3.3 MB, minified, **no sourcemaps** — zero `.map` files, zero `sourceMappingURL` in bundle). 386 JS chunks in `assets/`, heavy code-splitting (`chunk-agents-*`, `chunk-command-palette-*`, ...). `index.html` carries a strict CSP (`sand-avatar:`, `sand-media:` schemes).\n    | - **i18n:** lingui present (24 `catalog` refs, 46 `i18n` refs in bundle); `chunk-defaultLocale-C4B-KCzX.js` is a locale-number-format helper. **No separate `.po`/catalog JSON files shipped** — catalogs are inlined into chunks.\n    | - **0.18 reference frontend:** `refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reco...[preview truncated]\n\nWorkflow run: 83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c\nChild runs: scout-ref-anatomy=32ea0b37-53b3-4c92-bd8f-e9d72de464c5 (completed), scout-044-sources=bbe64187-187f-43a8-866e-6593b09f1b7d (completed), scout-delta-018-044=80df9860-691e-47df-97b5-68931c51a33d (completed), scout-native-render=8ca859cb-25c9-430e-9185-09e3e57fff74 (completed)"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"reasoning_content":"The workflow \"failed\" with a duplicate-key error — but all 4 children completed and wrote their files. The error is that `runs.all` re-referenced keys with the launch params... actually the error \"Duplicate workflow key 'scout-ref-anatomy' used with incompatible launch params\" — because I launched runs.run with agent/task params and then awaited via runs.all with just keys; runs.all probably re-resolves keys with incompatible (empty) params. Minor infrastructure issue; the children all completed and wrote outputs. Three files exist in analysis/rebuild-scout but scout-ref-anatomy.md is missing (only 3 files: delta, native-render, ref-anatomy... wait ls showed scout-delta, scout-native-render, scout-ref-anatomy — yes ref-anatomy.md exists 73 lines. And scout-044-sources.md missing from rebuild-scout dir? ls showed only 3 .md files: delta, native-render, ref-anatomy. The 044 output went to the sessions artifacts dir as scout-044-sources.md. Actually the receipt shows saved outputs in session artifacts. Fine — all 4 outputs are retrievable.\n\nAlso the scout-ref-anatomy output was saved at context.md and preview shows good content. Let me check the rebuild-scout dir for scout-044-sources.md missing — I should copy it. Let me check.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_79285ac197bd29f9fed4e3636b9e32d5","type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"cd \\\"/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/rebuild-scout\\\"; ls; A=\\\"/Users/panda/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-panda-Projects-test-local-grok-bot--/subagent-artifacts/outputs/83b3ebe0-dc71-4fea-a8cb-8a58707ce39c\\\"; cp -n \\\"$A/scout-044-sources.md\\\" . 2>/dev/null; ls; echo ---; head -30 scout-044-sources.md 2>/dev/null\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"scout-delta-018-044.md\nscout-native-render.md\nscout-ref-anatomy.md\nscout-044-sources.md\nscout-delta-018-044.md\nscout-native-render.md\nscout-ref-anatomy.md\n---\n# Scout 044 — Grok Bot 0.44.0 extracted sources survey\n\nRoots: `analysis/extracted/` (asar contents, 41 MB), `analysis/app.asar.unpacked/` (6.8 MB native/deps).\n\n## 1. dist/ tree & entry modules\n\n```\nextracted/dist/\n├── electron-main/            7.5M\n│   ├── main.cjs              12.7 KB  tiny bootstrap; minified but structured\n│   ├── main-core.cjs         1.73 MB  bundle (62 lines, minified, Sentry-wrapped)\n│   ├── main-app.cjs          2.04 MB  bundle (388 lines, minified)\n│   ├── chrome-import-worker.cjs  13 KB  worker bundle (minified)\n│   └── proto.cjs             4.06 MB  protobuf bundle (minified)\n├── electron-preload/\n│   ├── preload.cjs           66 KB   (minified, 3 lines)\n│   ├── preload-vnc.cjs       30 KB\n│   └── preload-webview.cjs   6.7 KB\n├── node-agent-coordinator/main.cjs   643 KB  (minified utilityProcess coordinator)\n├── local-exec-daemon/main.cjs        3.58 MB (minified standalone daemon)\n├── renderer/                 22 MB — index.html + 442 assets (386 chunk-*.js, KaTeX woff2, svg/png)\n├── deps/                     see manifest below\n└── native/                   sand-op-launcher (136 KB), sand-webauthn-signer (4.5 MB)\n```\n\nBootstrap mechanics (`main.cjs`): reads `main-core.cjs` / `main-app.cjs` and executes them via\n`vm.runInThisContext` (requires `node:vm`, `node:module`, `node:crypto`…). Error strings like\n\"main-core.cjs does not export remainderDue and noteStartupFailed\" and \"main-app.cjs does not\nexport reportMainCodeCache\" confirm these are CJS modules loaded by the bootstrap with\ncode-cache startup checks. No `utilityProcess.fork` string found in main.cjs itself; the\n","tool_call_id":"call_79285ac197bd29f9fed4e3636b9e32d5"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"reasoning_content":"All 4 scout outputs consolidated. The workflow itself threw a duplicate-key error at the runs.all step (infra quirk), but all 4 children completed and wrote files. Now I should synthesize the rebuild plan. Let me read the 4 files fully (they're small: 39-73 lines).","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2174901804a43b90b8ef90e382f7c7c1","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-ref-anatomy.md\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"# Scout: grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed anatomy (scaffold candidate for 0.44.0 rebuild)\n\nRepo: `/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main`\nNode engines `>=26.5.0 <27`; Electron devDep 42.1.0 (dev only — the shipped 0.18 shell is reused at package time); esbuild 0.28.2 bundler; TypeScript 7.0.2; vite for the reconstructed frontend only. **No electron-builder** — packaging is a fully custom Node pipeline.\n\n## 1. Top-level layout\n\n- `source/` — readable reconstructed TypeScript for all runtime processes (~80 KB LOC; see §2).\n- `src/app/` — the *staged upstream app payload*: `package.json` (name `sand`, version **0.18.0**, main `dist/electron-main/main.cjs`, `@anysphere/*` workspace deps) plus `dist/` hydrated from the checksum-pinned upstream `app.asar` by bootstrap (`scripts/lib/runtime.mjs:hydrateSourcePayloadFromAsar`). This is the asar staging root.\n- `frontend/` — partial evidence-backed reconstruction of the renderer (React/vite: `src/main.tsx`, `src/production/`, `src/recovered/`, `src/upstream.ts`, `manifests/renderer-*.json`). Used only for the \"clean-source\" renderer mode; NOT the shipped UI.\n- `manifests/reconstruction/` — `electron-main-production-bindings-manifest.json`, `renderer-closure.json`, `runner-parity-audit.json` (audit inputs, not build config).\n- `scripts/` — the entire build/package/verify toolchain (~7.4k LOC across 20 `.mjs` + `lib/`).\n- `tests/` — `node --test` suite (`node --test tests/*.test.mjs`): packaging, publication-bootstrap, updater-guard, router-settings, MCP/exec, inference-router tests.\n- `patches/` — one patchfile (`@connectrpc__connect@1.6.1.patch`) applied by `apply-third-party-patches.mjs` on postinstall.\n- `docs/` — `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PUBLISHING.md`, assets.\n- `research-archives/original/0.18.0/` — Git LFS preservation of the macOS arm64 DMG + Windows installer + `artifacts.json` + SHA256SUMS.\n- `PROVENANCE.md` (repo root) — upstream artifact identity & evidence-only rules.\n\n## 2. source/ per-process organization (ts LOC)\n\n| dir | ~LOC | key files |\n|---|---|---|\n| `electron-main/` | 16.3k | `main.ts`, `main-edge.ts`, `main-production-services.ts`, `production-binding-providers.ts`, `production-ipc-contract.ts`, subdirs: account, auth, box, coordinator, mcp, secrets, update, vnc, window-*, startup, telemetry, generated |\n| `electron-preload/` | 1.6k | `preload.ts` + `runtime/{primary,dev-controls,webview,vnc}.ts` entrypoints |\n| `electron-dev-controls/` | 167 | `main.ts` |\n| `host/` | **64.8k** (largest hand-written) | `main.ts`, `host-gateway-api.ts`, `gateway-server.ts`, `host-runner-composition.ts`, `sand-host.ts`, `sand-multitask.ts`, agents/, runner/, box/, local-exec/, mcp-auth/, storage/, workflows/ |\n| `node-agent-coordinator/` | 3.4k | `main.ts` (composeCoordinator), `inference-router.ts`, `renderer-port-server.ts`, `client-side-tool-v2-relay.ts`, `control-port-client.ts`, oauth/, gateway/, telemetry/ |\n| `local-exec-daemon/` | 514 | `main.ts` (runLocalExecDaemonEntrypoint) |\n| `box-exec-daemon/` | 537 | `main.ts`, `cli.ts` |\n| `packages/` | 337k | 31 `@anysphere/*` workspace libs: agent, agent-core, agent-exec, chat-inference(+proto), context(+rpc), mcp-core, proto, redaction, shell-exec, prompt-jsx, metrics, hooks*, etc. (mostly generated/proto-heavy) |\n| `shared/` | 16k | cross-process contracts: `transcript.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `local-exec-*.ts`, `gateway-wire.ts`, `inference-router.ts`, `update.ts`, rpc/, observability/ |\n| `internal/` | 426 | small internals |\n\n## 3. Build/packaging toolchain (custom, no electron-builder)\n\nPipeline (`npm run package` = check → `scripts/package-macos.mjs`):\n\n1. **bootstrap** (`scripts/bootstrap-runtime.mjs`) — downloads (or uses Git-LFS archive copy of) `Grok_Bot_0.18.0.dmg`, verifies SHA-256, mounts via hdiutil, caches `.cache/runtime/Grok Bot.app`, and extracts upstream `dist/` (electron-main main.cjs, host host-main.cjs, renderer) into `src/app/dist` after verifying upstream asar SHA-256.\n2. **clean build** (`scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs`) — esbuild-bundles each runtime entry from `source/` to CJS (`dist/electron-main/main.cjs`, `dist/host/host-main.cjs` fallback, preloads, workers, daemons, coordinator). Central **`runtimeComposition`** table declares per-runtime mode: `clean-source` | `artifact-fallback` (electron-main & host main still fall back to upstream artifacts!) | `artifact-runtime` (ABI-matched natives, `dist/deps`, `dist/native`, Electron shell copied from pinned runtime) | `generated-runtime`. Emits `dist/reconstruction-build.json` manifest with SHA-256 of every output.\n3. **overlay** — replaces upstream executables inside the staged `src/app` tree; packs ASAR via `scripts/lib/build-asar.mjs` + `asar-integrity.mjs` (staged-tree snapshot vs post-pack diff, `unpackedPrefixes = dist/deps|native|node-deps`).\n4. **renderer pinning** — two modes:\n   - *fidelity* (used by `package-macos.mjs`): shipped 0.18 renderer kept **byte-for-byte**; `createRendererArtifactProvenance()` writes `dist/renderer-artifact-provenance.json` — per-file `{path, bytes, sha256}` + `inventorySha256`, verified against embedded SHA-256 inventory.\n   - *clean-source*: vite/esbuild renderer from `frontend/`.\n   - **Hash-recorded settings transform** (`scripts/lib/router-renderer-patch.mjs`): exactly-once string-anchored patches on minified chunk(s) inject the Router settings panel + local-Docker toggle + usage panel; writes `dist/renderer-router-extension.json` recording original/patched bytes+sha256 per chunk. Fails hard if anchors are missing/ambiguous (these anchors are 0.18-minifier-specific and WILL differ in 0.44).\n5. **package** (`package-macos.mjs`) — `ditto` cached runtime app → swap in built asar → `plutil`: **remove `ElectronAsarIntegrity`**, set `CFBundleIdentifier=com.anysphere.sand.reconstructed`, DisplayName, rewrite `CFBundleURLTypes` (only `sand` scheme) → strip `_CodeSignature`, ad-hoc codesign (with retry), verify deep/strict + `verifyReconstructedMacPackage`. Injects updater/telemetry guard banner (`SAND_DISABLE_UPDATES/SENTRY/TELEMETRY=1`, `build-asar.mjs:reconstructedUpdaterGuard`) and patches dev-seam anchors into the upstream electron-main (`enableReconstructedDevSeams`/`enableReconstructedRuntimeSeams` — exact string anchors from 0.18 minified code).\n   - NOTE: `runtimeComposition` still marks electron-main and host main as `artifact-fallback` — the shipped 0.18 binaries are the actual runtime; `source/electron-main` & `source/host/main.ts` are built to `dist/recovered-source/` for parity audit only.\n\n## 4. Provenance / manifests\n\n- `PROVENANCE.md`: DMG URL + SHA-256 (`a253ccd8…`), upstream asar SHA-256 (`6665408…`), Windows installer hash, evidence-only reconstruction rules.\n- `research-archives/original/0.18.0/artifacts.json` + `SHA256SUMS` + LFS binaries.\n- Build-emitted manifests: `dist/reconstruction-build.json` (inputs, runtimeComposition, per-file sha256), `dist/renderer-artifact-provenance.json` (renderer inventory), `dist/renderer-router-extension.json` (patch deltas), `dist/deps/runtime-deps-manifest.json` (+ resolutionClosure byte-exact copies).\n- `manifests/reconstruction/*` audit manifests + `scripts/audit-renderer-closure.mjs`, `audit-runtime-composition.mjs`, `audit-ui-provenance.mjs`, `verify.mjs`, `verify-publication-tree.mjs`.\n\n## 5. 0.18-specific gates a 0.44.0 rebuild must change\n\n- `scripts/lib/config.mjs`: `upstreamVersion=\"0.18.0\"`, `dmgUrl`, `dmgSha256`, `upstreamAsarSha256`, bundle IDs/names (\"Grok Bot 0.18 Reconstructed\"), cached/archived DMG paths, `GROK_BOT_018_APP` env name.\n- `scripts/lib/runtime.mjs:validateRuntimeApp` — requires `CFBundleShortVersionString === upstreamVersion`.\n- `research-archives/original/0.18.0/` paths + `hydrateSourcePayloadFromAsar` required-file list (`dist/electron-main/main.cjs`, `dist/host/host-main.cjs`, `dist/renderer/index.html` — verify these paths still hold in 0.44 asar).\n- `scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs`: `createRendererArtifactProvenance` hardcodes `upstreamVersion: \"0.18.0\"`; `upstreamAsarSha256` from `macos-shell-invariant.mjs`; string-anchor patches (dev seams, runtime seams, renderer router patch) reference 0.18 minified tokens — must be re-derived from the 0.44 bundle.\n- Electron shell reuse means 0.44's own Electron version (check 0.44 CFBundleVersion) replaces the pinned 42.1.0 shell; `external: [\"electron\"]` bundling unaffected.\n- `src/app/package.json` version `0.18.0` and workspace dep list must be re-hydrated from 0.44 asar.\n- ABI assumptions: native `dist/deps`, `dist/native`, `dist/node-deps` (tree-sitter rebuilt via `build-tree-sitter-{electron,node}.mjs`) must match the 0.44 Electron/Node ABIs.\n\n## Start Here\n`scripts/lib/config.mjs` (all pinned constants) → `scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs` (`runtimeComposition`, lines 37–77) → `scripts/package-macos.mjs`.\n\n## Top 5 load-bearing facts\n1. Packaging is a fully custom Node pipeline (bootstrap→esbuild clean build→ASAR overlay→plutil/bundle-id swap→ad-hoc codesign); no electron-builder; the *upstream .app shell* (Electron framework + natives) is reused, only `app.asar` is rebuilt.\n2. Everything is keyed on checksum-pinned upstream artifacts (DMG sha, asar sha) in `scripts/lib/config.mjs` + `PROVENANCE.md`; 0.44 rebuild = swap these constants + re-hydrate `src/app/dist`.\n3. `runtimeComposition` in `scripts/lib/clean-build.mjs:37` is the build contract: preloads, daemons, coordinator, workers, renderer are `clean-source`; electron-main & host main are still `artifact-fallback` (upstream binaries); deps/natives/shell are `artifact-runtime`.\n4. Shipped renderer is kept byte-for-byte in \"fidelity\" mode with a per-file SHA-256 inventory (`renderer-artifact-provenance.json`), and the only UI change is an exactly-once, hash-recorded string-anchor patch (`router-renderer-patch.mjs`) whose anchors are 0.18-minifier-specific — must be re-derived for 0.44.\n5. Multiple brittle exact-string patches (dev/runtime seams, ElectronAsarIntegrity removal, updater-guard injection) assume 0.18 minified output; each will hard-fail against 0.44 and needs new anchors — these, plus the version/URL/hash constants, are the real porting work.\n","tool_call_id":"call_2174901804a43b90b8ef90e382f7c7c1"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_b1e26c4c41c6128151eac35720164f5a","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-delta-018-044.md\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"# Scout delta: 0.18 reconstruction sources ↔ 0.44.0 evidence\n\n0.18 tree: `refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main/source` (TS reconstruction; `src/` contains only a stub `app/package.json` — **no frontend source**).\n0.44 evidence: `analysis/RE-REPORT.md`, `analysis/sections/sec-{main,daemon,coord,native,render}.md`, `analysis/extracted/` (minified dist bundles).\n\n## Subsystem verdict table\n\n| Subsystem | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| electron-main | **Evolved** (mostly same, cookie import is new) | 0.18 has 185 files incl. `update/update-feed.ts`, `deep-link/`, `onepassword/`, `secrets/`, `box/`. 0.44 adds `chrome-import-worker.cjs` (saltysalt/1003-iter AES-128-CBC import) — **zero** cookie-import hits in 0.18 tree |\n| electron-preload | **Evolved** | 0.18 has `preload.ts`, `preload-vnc.ts`, `preload-webview.ts`, `passkey-stall.ts` etc. 0.44 evidence confirms same 3 preloads (desktop 189 RPC methods, noVNC beacon, webview IME); minor surface growth |\n| node-agent-coordinator | **Evolved (slightly)** | 0.18: 24 files, webauthn signer/provider, gateway/, local-exec supervisor. 0.44: 98 coordinator methods, 3 MessageChannels, WebAuthn SSE proxy `/webauthn/requests`+`/responses` — same architecture; count/registry drift only |\n| local-exec-daemon | **Evolved** | 0.18: 4 files (main, production-executor, invariant-violation-log). 0.44: 40-tool surface, 3 sandbox policies (seatbelt/landlock/win32-proxy), lease GC — same design, much larger tool registry |\n| box-exec-daemon | **Present in both / likely unchanged role** | 0.18: `box-exec-daemon/{main,server,cli}.ts`. 0.44 evidence covers it under anyrun/in-box process supervisor (`x-anyrun-network-token` in both trees) |\n| host | **Evolved** | 0.18: 471 files, full runner/tools/extensions. 0.44 unchanged at the architectural level (Temporal harness enums exist in 0.18 proto); new 0.44 host-side features are voice-call harness + routing knobs |\n| packages | **Evolved substantially** | 0.18: 31 packages, GrokBotService = **30 RPCs**, Dashboard 601, aiserver 192, bc 194. 0.44: GrokBotService **136**, Dashboard **660**, bc 226, AiService 194, SandBoxService **39 (new split)**, Analytics 8; total 1,263 methods, 5,594 proto msgs |\n| frontend | **New (missing in 0.18)** | 0.18 `src/` = one stub package.json; no renderer source. 0.44 evidence: React 19 + TipTap + 2,248-string i18n catalog, 32 settings panes — must be built from `analysis/extracted/dist/renderer` alone |\n\n## Flagged constants\n\n- **Bundle id / tracks**: 0.44 `com.anysphere.sand`, schemes `grokbot`+`sand`, tracks `sand`/`sand-nightly`/`sand-dogfood`. 0.18 has identical track mapping (`update-feed.ts:8,13`) and `com.anysphere.sand` **nowhere** in 0.18 tree (bundle id only in 0.44 evidence) → unchanged logic, id constant needs adding from evidence.\n- **Update feed**: `https://api2.cursor.sh/updates` — byte-identical in both (`DEFAULT_UPDATE_BASE_URL`, `update-feed.ts:6` vs sec-main.md L51). **Unchanged**.\n\n## New-in-0.44 with NO counterpart in the 0.18 tree\n\n1. **Voice calls** — `@anysphere/grok-bot-voice-call-harness` (0.44 package.json), `grok-voice-latest`/`grok-voice-think-fast-2.0`, `wss://api.x.ai/` dial, credential minting in main-app. 0.18: 0 files matching voice-call/`wss://`; only incidental \"voice\" words in a tool description.\n2. **GrokBotService split**: 30 → 136 methods, plus **SandBoxService (39 methods)** as strict subset — 0.18 has only the 30-method GrokBotService (`packages/proto/generated/aiserver/v1/grok_bot_connect.ts:10`).\n3. **`CUGrokBotService`** computer-use sidecar app (bundle `co.anysphere.grok-bot-computer-use`, JSON-RPC over unix socket, ffmpeg recording) — 0 hits in 0.18.\n4. **Chrome cookie import** — `chrome-import-worker.cjs`, `chrome-cookie-import` settings id, Full Disk Access gating — 0 hits in 0.18.\n5. **Native Rust binaries** `sand-webauthn-signer` + `sand-op-launcher` — 0.18 has the **JS driver** side (`node-agent-coordinator/webauthn/signer.ts`, `electron-main/onepassword/onepassword-cli-runtime.ts` incl. identical codesign req `OU 2BUA8C4S2C`), but the compiled Mach-O helpers themselves appear only in 0.44 evidence (sec-native.md §1.2–1.3, CTAP2/authenticator-0.5.0). JS contracts match; native crates need fresh reconstruction.\n6. **anyrun.v1 protocol expansion** — 0.18 already has `packages/proto/generated/anyrun/v1/` (pod, pod_daemon, snapshot, persisted_dev_container); 0.44 documents 171 messages + `CreateProcess`/restart-backoff/pod-metrics + `x-anyrun-network-token` header → **evolved, not new**, but message set must be diffed.\n7. **`grokbot://` template deep links** — the route table (`/v1/agent`, `/v1/bot-template` id=`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{21}$`, `/v1/marketplace`, `/v1/plugin/add`, `/v1/github-connect-callback`, `/v1/open`, `/v1/settings` (26 ids), `/v1/sidebar`) is documented only from 0.44 main-core.cjs; 0.18 has the controller machinery (`electron-main/deep-link/deep-link-controller.ts`, `shared/deep-link.ts`) but **no reconstructed route table** → partially new / needs completion.\n8. **Temporal harness mode enum** — `GrokBotAgentHarnessKind{BOX,TEMPORAL}`, `GrokBotTemporalHarnessMode{OFF,SHADOW,LIVE,BOX}` exist in 0.44 evidence; 0.18 has only a single Temporal mention (memory-synthesis-service.ts) and the enums were **not found** in the 0.18 grok_bot proto → likely new in 0.44 (verify in 0.44 proto.cjs).\n9. **Renderer/i18n catalog** — entirely absent from 0.18 (`src/` stub). 2,248 strings, 32 settings surfaces, voice/dictation UI, template share UI all fresh.\n10. **Models & plans surface** — `grok-4.5`/`grok-4.6`, `grok-bot-computer-use` (+lab/dev), `grok-transcribe` 24 kHz, Grok Bot Plan / SuperGrok Lite/Plus/Heavy — not present as constants in 0.18 tree.\n\n## Key 0.18 anchors for rebuild\n\n- `source/electron-main/update/update-feed.ts:1-30` — feed URL, tracks, platform ids, response kinds (all confirmed unchanged in 0.44).\n- `source/node-agent-coordinator/webauthn/signer.ts:1-25` — `[signer-event] ` protocol, SignerEvent union (matches 0.44 sec-native exactly).\n- `source/electron-main/onepassword/onepassword-cli-runtime.ts:1-14` — managed op CLI 2.35.0, codesign requirements (matches 0.44).\n- `source/packages/proto/generated/aiserver/v1/grok_bot_connect.ts:10-59` — old 30-method GrokBotService (EnsureSandBox family) that 0.44 expanded to 136.\n- `source/electron-main/deep-link/deep-link-controller.ts` — dedupe/pending-queue dispatch (0.44 keeps it; route table new).\n\n## Start here\n\n`analysis/sections/sec-coord.md` §2 (protobuf surface) + 0.44 `extracted/dist/electron-main/proto.cjs` — the 1,263-method RPC delta is the single largest reconstruction gap; everything else wires into it.\n","tool_call_id":"call_b1e26c4c41c6128151eac35720164f5a"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6cc923c6e6837d18fec29be7b72c5641","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/Users/panda/Projects/test-local/grok-bot/analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-native-render.md\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"# Scout: Native/Sidecar + Renderer — grok-bot 0.44.0 vs 0.18 reconstruction\n\n## A. Native binaries\n\n### `analysis/app.asar.unpacked/dist/native/` (2 files)\n\n| Binary | Type | Language | Role | 0.18 equivalent |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `sand-op-launcher` | Mach-O universal (x86_64 + arm64), executable | Native (no Rust/Swift runtime strings found; small hardened launcher) | Hardened launcher/wrapper for 1Password CLI (`op`): codesign-verifies `com.1password.op` (team `2BUA8C4S2C`), sandbox_init profile restricting App Data access, env scrubbing (`OP_CACHE=false`, `OP_BIOMETRIC_UNLOCK_ENABLED=true`, `OP_LOAD_DESKTOP_APP_SETTINGS=false`), `account list --format=json`, service-account token creation. Strings: \"untrusted 1Password CLI\", \"1Password CLI changed before launch\" | **TS orchestration exists, launcher binary itself does not.** 0.18 has `source/electron-main/onepassword/onepassword-cli-runtime.ts` + `onepassword-cli-dev-controls.ts` which *expect* a launcher at `dist/native/` and codesign-verify it (constant `SAND_OP_LAUNCHER_IDENTIFIER_REQUIREMENT = 'identifier \"sand-op-launcher\"'`). No Rust/launcher source in the 0.18 tree (`find -name '*.rs'` = none) |\n| `sand-webauthn-signer` | Mach-O universal (x86_64 + arm64), executable | **Rust** (strings show `crates/sand-webauthn-signer/src/main.rs`, aes 0.8.4 / getrandom crates, `sand-release-cargo-home`, built on Anysphere Buildkite CI) | CTAP2/FIDO2 security-key signer: parse DER/CBOR (`IndefiniteLengthTagNumber`, `unexpected key`), operations makeCred/getAssertion, PIN/UV states (`PresenceRequired`, `force_pin_change`, `UserVerification`), emits signer-event lines | **TS side only.** 0.18 `source/node-agent-coordinator/webauthn/signer.ts` (line 47: `SIGNER_BINARY = ... \"sand-webauthn-signer\"`) spawns and parses this binary's event stream (presence-required / pin-not-set / pin-blocked / uv-* events match the Rust binary's strings exactly). No Rust sources (`crates/sand-webauthn-signer`) in the 0.18 tree — only the consumer. 0.18 `scripts/verify.mjs` line 58 merely requires the *built binary* to exist |\n\n**Verdict:** both native executables are **opaque binaries — treat as prebuilt, reuse from 0.44 build as-is** (they are self-contained, codesigned wrappers/signers). The *Node-side protocol* is fully recoverable from 0.18 TS sources (`signer.ts`, `onepassword-cli-runtime.ts`), so integration glue can be rebuilt; the Rust crates cannot (sources never published).\n\n### `analysis/extracted/dist/deps/`\n\n| Entry | Contents | 0.18 equivalent |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cursor-proclist` | dir; `build/Release/cursor_proclist.node` — native Node addon (C/C++) | 0.18 has `scripts/build-tree-sitter-*.mjs` etc.; check `scripts/lib/*` + `patches/` — proclist addon is buildable via node-gyp if source in patches; else opaque |\n| `tree-sitter` | `build/Release/tree_sitter_runtime_binding.node` (node-gyp C addon) | 0.18 `scripts/build-tree-sitter-electron.mjs` + `build-tree-sitter-node.mjs` — **rebuildable from source** |\n| `tree-sitter-bash` | `prebuilds/darwin-arm64/tree-sitter-bash.node` | Same tree-sitter tooling; prebuild = stock npm package artifact |\n| `web-tree-sitter` | JS + `tree-sitter.wasm` | Stock npm package — reuse |\n| `node-addon-api`, `node-gyp-build` | Pure-JS npm helpers | Stock — reuse |\n| `runtime-deps-manifest.json` | Records required/copied/nodeFiles lists (see above) | Matches 0.18 packaging flow |\n\n## B. Renderer\n\n- **Bundle:** `analysis/extracted/dist/renderer/assets/index-C6zjACOA.js` (3.3 MB, minified, **no sourcemaps** — zero `.map` files, zero `sourceMappingURL` in bundle). 386 JS chunks in `assets/`, heavy code-splitting (`chunk-agents-*`, `chunk-command-palette-*`, ...). `index.html` carries a strict CSP (`sand-avatar:`, `sand-media:` schemes).\n- **i18n:** lingui present (24 `catalog` refs, 46 `i18n` refs in bundle); `chunk-defaultLocale-C4B-KCzX.js` is a locale-number-format helper. **No separate `.po`/catalog JSON files shipped** — catalogs are inlined into chunks.\n- **0.18 reference frontend:** `refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main/frontend/src` — 279 TS/TSX files, 3.3 MB readable source, split into `production/` (AgentRow, CommandPalette, ProductionRenderer, sidebar, settings…), `recovered/`, `dev/`. Entry `frontend/src/main.tsx`, built by `scripts/renderer-production-build.mjs` (vite + esbuild, deterministic banner, `renderer-source-provenance.json`, KaTeX hash pinning, `audit-renderer-closure.mjs` / `audit-ui-provenance.mjs` gates).\n- **Recovery tooling:** `scripts/recover-frontend.mjs` uses esbuild `transform` to de-minify/recover frontend files from a shipped bundle — this is the 0.18 method for regenerating readable TSX from minified output. `scripts/lib/router-renderer-patch.mjs` handles router/renderer patching.\n\n## Renderer strategy options for 0.44\n\n1. **Diff-and-patch (recommended):** reuse the 0.18 readable `frontend/src` as base, run 0.18's `recover-frontend.mjs`-style esbuild transform pipeline against 0.44's `index-C6zjACOA.js` + chunks to recover changed/new modules, diff against 0.18 sources, port deltas. Keeps readable source and 0.18 build tooling.\n2. **Treat 0.44 renderer as opaque:** ship the extracted `dist/renderer/` verbatim (no source needed unless preload/bridge contracts changed — verify against 0.18 `source/electron-preload/`).\n3. **Full re-derivation:** recover all 386 chunks to TSX — highest effort, sourcemap-less, poor ROI given option 1/2.\n\n## Start Here\n`refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main/scripts/recover-frontend.mjs` — it defines the proven recovery pipeline to rerun against 0.44's renderer bundle.\n","tool_call_id":"call_6cc923c6e6837d18fec29be7b72c5641"},{"role":"assistant","content":"All 4 scout findings are in (note: the workflow's final `runs.all` step hit an infra duplicate-key validation error, but every child completed and wrote its file — outputs recovered to `analysis/rebuild-scout/`). Writing the consolidated rebuild plan:","reasoning_content":"All 4 scouts done. Now synthesize the rebuild plan. The user's goal: \"start rebuild source code for Grok_Bot_0.44.0.dmg use reference from refrence/\". Phase 4 of the prompt.\n\nPlan synthesis:\n- Scaffold: fork/copy the 0.18 reconstruction repo as the scaffold, then port.\n- Key steps:\n  1. Create new repo (e.g. `grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed/`) from the 0.18 reference as template.\n  2. Update pinned constants in scripts/lib/config.mjs: version 0.44.0, DMG sha (compute), asar sha (compute), paths.\n  3. Re-hydrate src/app from analysis/extracted (already extracted).\n  4. Port source/ TS deltas: new modules (chrome-import worker TS, voice-call harness, coordinator method registry, 40-tool daemon registry, deep-link route table, proto packages update: GrokBotService 136, SandBoxService 39, anyrun diff).\n  5. Re-derive minified anchors: dev seams, runtime seams, ElectronAsarIntegrity, renderer router patch anchors — from 0.44 bundles.\n  6. Native: reuse 0.44 dist/native binaries as-is (opaque), JS driver from 0.18 sources.\n  7. Renderer: fidelity mode = byte-for-byte 0.44 renderer + new provenance inventory; compute new SHA-256 inventory.\n  8. Tests/verify re-run.\n\nShould I propose the plan and ask which scope? Per AGENTS.md: plan multi-step tasks, write plan to file first. Also ask questions one at a time. But user said \"start rebuild\". Best: write the plan file (REBUILD-PLAN.md) with phased tasks, then confirm scope choice — actually I could just proceed with recommended default (diff-and-patch renderer option 1, fidelity packaging). But this is a big multi-week effort. The reasonable move: present the consolidated plan + decisions, ask one question about which renderer strategy / how far to go (scaffold-only vs full port).\n\nAlso note the workflow infra error (duplicate key) — mention briefly that all 4 children completed despite the runs.all validation error, outputs recovered.\n\nLet me write analysis/REBUILD-PLAN.md, then present concise summary + one question.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7fc372c60a7a10e7807f09dbc67d56d7","type":"function","function":{"name":"write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"# Grok Bot 0.44.0 — Source Rebuild Plan\\n\\n**Scaffold:** `refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main` (0.18 reconstruction, per scout-ref-anatomy)\\n**Target:** `Grok_Bot_0.44.0.dmg` (asar already extracted in `analysis/extracted/`, natives in `analysis/app.asar.unpacked/`)\\n**Scout inputs:** `analysis/rebuild-scout/scout-{ref-anatomy,044-sources,delta-018-044,native-render}.md`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Strategy decision (recommended defaults)\\n\\n| Decision | Choice | Rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Scaffold reuse | Fork 0.18 reconstruction repo, port constants + anchors | Whole custom packaging pipeline (bootstrap→esbuild→asar overlay→codesign) transfers as-is |\\n| Renderer mode | **Fidelity** (ship 0.44 `dist/renderer/` byte-for-byte + new SHA-256 provenance inventory) | 386 minified chunks, no sourcemaps; full re-derivation is poor ROI. Optional later: diff-and-patch via 0.18 `recover-frontend.mjs` pipeline |\\n| Native binaries | Ship 0.44 `dist/native/{sand-webauthn-signer,sand-op-launcher}` + `dist/deps/*.node` as opaque `artifact-runtime` | Rust/C sources never published; 0.18 TS driver side (signer.ts, onepassword-cli-runtime.ts) already matches the 0.44 binary contracts |\\n| electron-main / host main | Keep `artifact-fallback` (upstream 0.44 binaries) initially, then upgrade to clean-source where 0.18 TS sources port cleanly | Matches the 0.18 repo's own runtimeComposition; clean-source porting is the long tail |\\n\\n## Phase A — Scaffold bootstrap (mechanical port)\\n\\n1. Copy `refrence/grok-bot-0.18-reconstructed-main` → `~/Projects/active/grok-bot-0.44-reconstructed/` (new git repo, not a submodule).\\n2. Compute identities: `shasum -a 256` on the DMG and on the extracted `app.asar` (re-asar from `analysis/extracted` or hash the original inside the DMG).\\n3. Update `scripts/lib/config.mjs`: `upstreamVersion=\\\"0.44.0\\\"`, `dmgUrl` (`https://downloads.cursor.com/grokbot/stable/darwin-arm64/0.44.0/Grok_Bot_0.44.0.dmg` — verify), `dmgSha256`, `upstreamAsarSha256`, bundle names/ids, cached DMG paths.\\n4. Re-hydrate `src/app/` from `analysis/extracted/` (0.44 asar `package.json` + `dist/`): version 0.44.0, ~35 `@anysphere/*` workspace deps, new deps list (`@anysphere/grok-bot-voice-call-harness` etc.), `dist/deps/runtime-deps-manifest.json`.\\n5. Verify `hydrateSourcePayloadFromAsar` required-file list against the 0.44 asar layout (`dist/electron-main/main.cjs`, `dist/renderer/index.html`; note 0.44 has no `dist/host/host-main.cjs` in asar — host lives where? verify).\\n6. PROVENANCE.md rewrite with 0.44 identities.\\n\\n## Phase B — Anchor re-derivation (the brittle part)\\n\\nEvery exact-string patch keyed to 0.18 minified output must be re-derived against 0.44 bundles:\\n\\n- `enableReconstructedDevSeams` / `enableReconstructedRuntimeSeams` anchors → re-find in `main-core.cjs`/`main-app.cjs` (Sentry-wrapped, minified).\\n- `ElectronAsarIntegrity` removal, updater/telemetry guard injection → same.\\n- Renderer router/settings patch anchors → 0.44 chunk names are semantic (`chunk-settings`, `chunk-agents`, …); re-derive anchors or park the settings transform for phase 1 (ship un-patched renderer).\\n- Renderer provenance inventory: regenerate `renderer-artifact-provenance.json` over the 442 0.44 renderer assets.\\n\\n## Phase C — Source delta port (the substance)\\n\\nSubsystem verdicts (from scout-delta):\\n\\n| Subsystem | 0.18→0.44 action |\\n|---|---|\\n| electron-preload | port as-is; verify 3-preload surface against 0.44 preload.cjs/preload-vnc.cjs/preload-webview.cjs |\\n| node-agent-coordinator | port + update method registry (98 methods, 3 MessageChannels, WebAuthn SSE proxy `/webauthn/requests`+`/responses`) |\\n| local-exec-daemon | port + expand to 40-tool registry + 3 sandbox policies + lease GC (evidence: sec-daemon.md, `local-exec-daemon/main.cjs` 3.58 MB) |\\n| box-exec-daemon / anyrun | port; diff `anyrun.v1` message set (0.18 partial → 0.44 has 171 msgs, CreateProcess, restart-backoff, pod metrics) |\\n| electron-main | port + new: `chrome-import-worker` TS (Chrome cookie decrypt: keychain → PBKDF2 \\\"saltysalt\\\" ×1003 → AES-128-CBC; TCC/Finder workaround), deep-link route table (`grokbot://` `/v1/agent|bot-template|marketplace|plugin/add|github-connect-callback|open|settings|sidebar`), voice-call credential minting |\\n| host | port as-is + voice-call harness knobs |\\n| packages/proto | **largest gap**: GrokBotService 30→136, new SandBoxService 39, Dashboard 601→660, bc 194→226, Analytics 8, AiService 194, total 1,263 methods / 5,594 msgs — regenerate proto surface from 0.44 `dist/electron-main/proto.cjs` (4.06 MB) + `sec-coord.md` §2 |\\n| Temporal harness | new enums `GrokBotAgentHarnessKind{BOX,TEMPORAL}`, `GrokBotTemporalHarnessMode{OFF,SHADOW,LIVE,BOX}` — add to proto/daemon |\\n| CUGrokBotService | new sidecar (JSON-RPC unix socket, ffmpeg recording) — reconstruct from evidence only |\\n| Models/plans constants | `grok-4.5/4.6`, `grok-voice-*`, `grok-bot-computer-use`, `grok-transcribe`, SuperGrok Lite/Plus/Heavy |\\n| Renderer | phase 1: fidelity byte-for-byte; later: diff-and-patch recovery |\\n\\n## Phase D — Assemble, verify, iterate\\n\\n1. `npm run package` (custom pipeline) with 0.44 runtime app cached from the mounted DMG.\\n2. Re-run `tests/` (node --test) — update fixture constants (0.18→0.44 hashes, version gates).\\n3. Verify: ad-hoc codesign deep/strict, asar integrity snapshot, renderer provenance, runtime composition audit.\\n4. Log every string-anchor