);\n\nexport const fidelityRuntimeComposition = Object.freeze(runtimeComposition.map(runtime => (\n  runtime.runtime === \"renderer\" ? Object.freeze({\n    runtime: \"renderer\",\n    path: \"dist/renderer\",\n    mode: \"checksum-pinned-artifact-runtime\",\n    artifactRoot: \"src/app/dist/renderer\",\n","tool_call_id":"call_2765e4315c061822082c41a04a66aa39"},{"role":"assistant","content":"0.18 asar shipped `dist/host/` (host-main + workers); 0.44's doesn't — the host role moved into `dist/local-exec-daemon/main.cjs` (3.58 MB standalone). Composition/hydrate contracts need a 0.44 profile. Reading the pinned constants:","reasoning_content":"Now I understand the runtimeComposition contract fully. In 0.18's asar, `dist/host/` existed (host-main.cjs + workers). In 0.44's asar, there's no `dist/host` — the 0.44 local-exec-daemon (3.58MB) presumably absorbed the host role, or host lives elsewhere. Let me quickly check what 0.18's asar had — the reference's src/app/dist is hydrated from 0.18 asar. Check src/app/dist existence: earlier ls src/app showed only package.json (dist is hydrated at build time, not committed). The hydrate list confirms 0.18 asar had dist/host/host-main.cjs.\n\nFor 0.44: the hydrate required list must become: dist/electron-main/main.cjs, dist/node-agent-coordinator/main.cjs, dist/local-exec-daemon/main.cjs, dist/renderer/index.html, dist/electron-preload/preload.cjs, dist/native/... etc. And runtimeComposition needs a 0.44 profile. But careful: don't rewrite the whole build contract yet — Phase A is constants + hydration; Phase C reworks composition.\n\nAlso verify 0.18 vs 0.44 asar layouts to see exactly what dirs differ. 0.18 asar — can I inspect? The DMG is LFS-preserved in reference research-archives (only 20K → manifests only, binaries via LFS pointers maybe not present). Can't inspect 0.18 asar locally without downloading. Skip; rely on hydrate list.\n\nNow do the mechanical Phase A work:\n1. Update scripts/lib/config.mjs constants (version,